==English==

===Etymology===
A variant of {{m|en|registery}},<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=1133616870}}</ref> from {{inh|en|enm|regestery|t=?a record book; ?a bookmark}},<ref name="MED">{{R:MED Online|entry=reǧisterī|pos=n|id=MED36500}}</ref> partly from {{der|en|la-med|regesterium}}, {{m|la|registerium}}<ref name="MED"/><ref name="OED">{{R:OED Online|entry=registery|pos=n|id=1203871996}}</ref> and probably also partly formed with {{affix|en|-ery}}.<ref name="OED"/> Equivalent to {{af|en|register|-y|id2=noun}}.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|pos=n|v=37023}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɛd͡ʒɪstɹi/|a=RP,GA,CA}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-registry.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹed͡ʒɪstɹi/|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{wp}}
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} A building in which things are [[registered]] or where [[register]]s are kept.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[record]]; an [[account]]; a [[register]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|title=Bride's Book of Etiquette (Revised)|page=276
|passage=The best — and easiest — way to shop for the "perfect" gift is to consult the couple's wedding gift '''registry''', since these are the items they want and need {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The act of [[registering]]; [[registration]].
# {{lb|en|countable|computing}} A [[database]] of [[configuration]] settings etc. maintained by the {{w|Microsoft Windows}} [[operating system]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=John Papa; C. Caison; Matt Brown|title=Professional ADO RDS programming with ASP|page=252
|passage=To unregister a DLL and remove the corresponding entries from the '''registry''', add the <code>/u</code> switch to the command {{...}}}}

